<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco cuts most bunker prices by $2/tonne.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco cuts most bunker prices by $2/tonne.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has cut the price of A-960 bunker fuel by $2 a tonne to $124 ($19.03 a barrel) from Gulf ports and $128 ($19.65) from Red Sea ports, the firm said.</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel grade is also cut by $2 to $223 from Ras Tanura and Dammam though liftings from Jeddah and Yanbu are left unchanged at $225 a tonne.</p>
<p>Prices are effective November 21.</p>
</text>
